From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wangao Wang <wangao.wang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:12:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] media: iris: fix ltr count rc_type validity check in
 gen2

The condition was inverted: CBR_VFR, CBR_CFR and RC_OFF are the valid
rc_types for LTR, so reject anything that does NOT match these types.

Fixes: 6870381285b8 ("media: qcom: iris: Add Long-Term Reference support for encoder")
Signed-off-by: Wangao Wang <wangao.wang@oss.qualcomm.com>

[mzak: picked from lore <20261029-gen2_ltr_fix-v1-1-6d5518d59b9c@oss.qualcomm.com> for q91j, gains #30; applies unchanged]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
index 46d47c3a6..2612907ae 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
@@ -1430,9 +1430,9 @@ int iris_set_ltr_count_gen2(struct iris_inst *inst, enum platform_inst_fw_cap_ty
 	if (!ltr_count)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (inst->hfi_rc_type == HFI_RC_CBR_VFR ||
-	    inst->hfi_rc_type == HFI_RC_CBR_CFR ||
-	    inst->hfi_rc_type == HFI_RC_OFF) {
+	if (inst->hfi_rc_type != HFI_RC_CBR_VFR &&
+	    inst->hfi_rc_type != HFI_RC_CBR_CFR &&
+	    inst->hfi_rc_type != HFI_RC_OFF) {
 		inst->fw_caps[LTR_COUNT].value = 0;
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
-- 
